# HOM-347: example env for the `graph/` LangGraph project.
#
# Two distinct use cases — keep them separate:
#
# 1. `langgraph dev` on the dev box (default Phase 3 / Phase 4 work).
#    Loads `graph/.env` per `graph/langgraph.json`. No secrets required.
#    Thread state lives in `.langgraph_api/.langgraph_checkpoint.*.pckl` and
#    does NOT survive hard restarts on Windows (HOM-346 empirical).
#
# 2. TrueNAS-deployed Self-Hosted Lite stack (HOM-347, for step-debug
#    walkthroughs that need restart-resumable threads). The server-side
#    `.env` lives at /var/lib/homestudio-langgraph/.env on TrueNAS,
#    NOT in this repo. Push the template with `./deploy.sh --secrets`.
#
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# LangSmith API key — REQUIRED for the TrueNAS stack ONLY
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Get a free Developer-tier key at https://smith.langchain.com → Settings
# → API Keys. The Self-Hosted Lite plan is what runs on TrueNAS via
# `langchain/langgraph-api`. The key is validated on every server boot.
#
# This is operator-supplied and lives on the server, NOT in this repo:
#   /var/lib/homestudio-langgraph/.env
# Push a template there with: ./deploy.sh --secrets
#
# LANGSMITH_API_KEY=lsv2_...
# LANGSMITH_PROJECT=homestudio-langgraph

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Enterprise upgrade (NOT what HOM-347 ships) — only if you license it
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# `LANGGRAPH_CLOUD_LICENSE_KEY` swaps the Self-Hosted Lite license for a
# full Enterprise license. We do not use this; documented here only so
# operators know it exists. Self-Hosted Lite (Developer-tier LangSmith
# key) is the supported path.
#
# LANGGRAPH_CLOUD_LICENSE_KEY=...
